TEST(1)                       User Commands

NAME
    test - evaluate a condition

SYNOPSIS
    test expression
    [ expression ]

DESCRIPTION
    Returns 0 for true, 1 for false and 2 for an invalid builtin expression.
    The shell builtin supports = != < >, -eq -ne -lt -le -gt -ge,
    -z -n, -e -f -d -b -c -r -w -x -s -t, !, parentheses, -a and -o.
    Quote expanded values and escape parentheses and < > from the shell.
    The standalone /bin/test supports the basic string, integer and file
    tests; the builtin is used by default.

SEE ALSO
    sh(1), man(1), index(7)
